whisper: Every engine word, for the engine checks (engines/*/check/check.py). The scene: Mover at 1 horizontal 2 vertical 3 depth,
whisper: Box (no program), Target (this program too) and Player, a ball falling onto Target. expected.txt is what it must say.
use: engine
use: maths

the world remembers:
  frames (a number)
  hits (a number)
and the universe said i love you

to begin:
  if object name of me is "Mover":
    show every word
and the universe said i love you

to show every word:
  scrawl "name ", object name of me
  scrawl "start ", place of me
  put the object with me, 4 horizontal 5 vertical 6 depth
  scrawl "put ", place of me
  move the object with me, 1 horizontal 0 vertical 0 depth
  scrawl "moved ", place of me
  turn the object with me, 90
  scrawl "turn ", round (turn of me)
  set box to the object named "Box"
  scrawl "box ", object name of box
  scrawl "nobody ", the object named "Nobody"
  set made to copy the object with (box, 0 horizontal 10 vertical 0 depth)
  scrawl "copy ", place of made, " ", made is not box
  remove the object made
  colour the object with box, "blue"
  scrawl "keys ", key held "space", " ", key pressed "space"
  scrawl "frame time ", frame time is at least 0
  scrawl "problem next"
  scrawl place of 0
  scrawl "not reached"
and the universe said i love you

to every frame, given seconds (a number):
  if object name of me is "Mover":
    set frames to frames plus 1
    if frames is 10:
      scrawl "frames 10 ", seconds exceeds 0
and the universe said i love you

to touched, given other (a number):
  set hits to hits plus 1
  if hits is 1:
    scrawl "touched ", object name of me, " by ", object name of other
    colour the object with other, "red"
and the universe said i love you
